WEBVTT

00:00:00.254 --> 00:00:02.784
Mia, the toy slows down and stops.

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:04.648
Has all its energy disappeared?

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:10.365
It looks as if the energy has been used
up, but that is probably the phrase that

00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:12.411
makes you reach for an imaginary tissue.

00:00:13.244 --> 00:00:14.094
Exactly.

00:00:14.479 --> 00:00:15.955
Energy is conserved.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.727
In our ordinary physical systems, it is
transferred between stores or across a

00:00:20.727 --> 00:00:23.602
system boundary, not created or destroyed.

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:27.012
When the toy stops, we must
trace where its energy went.

00:00:27.753 --> 00:00:31.220
Some has spread into internal
stores of the toy and surroundings

00:00:31.221 --> 00:00:34.640
through friction, and some may
have been carried away by sound.

00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:35.961
Correct.

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:37.884
Energy is measured in joules.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.403
One kilojoule is 1,000 joules.

00:00:40.757 --> 00:00:43.667
Degrees Celsius measure
temperature, and watts measure

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:45.537
power, not the amount of energy.

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:49.107
Why do you keep saying system boundary?

00:00:49.769 --> 00:00:52.748
Because the toy alone can lose
energy to its surroundings

00:00:52.748 --> 00:00:54.477
without violating conservation.

00:00:54.973 --> 00:00:58.548
For an isolated system, total
energy remains constant.

00:00:58.878 --> 00:01:02.628
If energy enters or leaves the
system we chose, our accounting

00:01:02.643 --> 00:01:04.412
must include those transfers.

00:01:05.272 --> 00:01:08.655
So an object's energy can decrease
while the total is conserved.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.271
Lost from the toy does not
mean destroyed from existence

00:01:12.646 --> 00:01:14.765
Our course uses eight energy stores.

00:01:15.236 --> 00:01:18.564
Start with a moving cyclist, a
book raised above the floor, and a

00:01:18.564 --> 00:01:24.562
compressed spring Kinetic, gravitational
potential, and elastic potential.

00:01:24.944 --> 00:01:28.331
More speed means more kinetic
energy for the same mass.

00:01:28.837 --> 00:01:31.555
Raising the book increases
the gravitational potential

00:01:31.555 --> 00:01:33.513
energy of the Earth-book system

00:01:34.272 --> 00:01:34.654
Good.

00:01:35.043 --> 00:01:38.881
The reference height matters when we
assign gravitational potential energy.

00:01:39.241 --> 00:01:43.672
A compressed or stretched elastic object
can transfer energy back when released.

00:01:44.052 --> 00:01:48.020
These stores describe arrangements
and motion, not invisible liquids

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:53.217
inside objects Food, fuel, and
a charged battery are examples

00:01:53.217 --> 00:01:56.435
associated with chemical stores Yes.

00:01:56.581 --> 00:01:58.092
Here is a chemistry trap.

00:01:58.502 --> 00:02:00.608
Breaking chemical bonds requires energy.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:02.661
Forming bonds releases energy.

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:06.099
A reaction releases energy overall
when the energy released in

00:02:06.099 --> 00:02:09.480
forming new bonds exceeds that
required to break the old ones

00:02:10.223 --> 00:02:13.422
So energy is not released
merely by snapping a bond

00:02:13.446 --> 00:02:14.977
like opening a treasure chest.

00:02:15.366 --> 00:02:18.282
I need to consider the whole
reaction and its products

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:19.827
Exactly.

00:02:20.393 --> 00:02:23.857
Next, internal energy is
associated with microscopic

00:02:23.866 --> 00:02:25.801
particle motion and interactions.

00:02:26.203 --> 00:02:29.461
Objects have internal energy
even when they feel cold to us.

00:02:29.742 --> 00:02:32.044
It is not only the
motion of warm particles

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:35.676
Nuclear energy involves atomic nuclei.

00:02:36.146 --> 00:02:39.493
Electrostatic and magnetic
stores involve arrangements of

00:02:39.494 --> 00:02:41.513
charges and magnetic systems.

00:02:41.954 --> 00:02:45.162
That gives all eight stores Correct.

00:02:45.478 --> 00:02:50.493
Kinetic, gravitational, elastic,
chemical, internal, nuclear,

00:02:50.592 --> 00:02:52.627
electrostatic, and magnetic.

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:57.024
Light, sound, and electrical
transfer are not extra stores in

00:02:57.024 --> 00:02:58.377
this school bookkeeping scheme

00:02:59.306 --> 00:03:02.943
A battery is not best described
as a tank of electrical energy.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:07.327
Chemical changes allow it to transfer
energy electrically into a circuit

00:03:07.683 --> 00:03:08.532
I lift a book.

00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:12.330
What increases and how
is energy transferred?

00:03:13.102 --> 00:03:15.515
The gravitational
potential store increases.

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:19.717
Your force moves the book, so
energy is transferred mechanically.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.458
Your body's chemical processes
supply the energy for the action.

00:03:24.225 --> 00:03:24.592
Good.

00:03:25.059 --> 00:03:29.013
In a kettle, energy is transferred
electrically to the element and by

00:03:29.014 --> 00:03:30.905
heating to the water and surroundings.

00:03:31.272 --> 00:03:33.597
The water's internal energy increases.

00:03:33.845 --> 00:03:36.907
The supply connection is a
pathway, not a named store.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.970
When sunlight reaches a solar
panel, energy is transferred

00:03:40.984 --> 00:03:42.865
by electromagnetic radiation.

00:03:43.277 --> 00:03:44.508
That can cross a vacuum.

00:03:45.322 --> 00:03:45.873
Correct.

00:03:46.216 --> 00:03:49.508
We commonly describe transfer
mechanically, electrically,

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.833
by heating, and by radiation.

00:03:52.224 --> 00:03:56.307
Thermal radiation may also be described
as a heating mechanism, depending on

00:03:56.308 --> 00:03:58.511
how the course organizes its categories.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.090
Be explicit about the physical process.

00:04:01.865 --> 00:04:03.111
Where does sound fit?

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.862
It carries energy, but it
cannot travel through a vacuum.

00:04:07.718 --> 00:04:11.336
Sound is a mechanical wave
transferring energy through matter,

00:04:11.602 --> 00:04:13.598
not electromagnetic radiation.

00:04:14.131 --> 00:04:17.679
A diagram can label its arrow
sound waves but should not add a

00:04:17.679 --> 00:04:19.436
permanent sound store at the end.

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:20.618
Then

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:24.587
I show the final internal stores after
the vibrations have been absorbed.

00:04:25.055 --> 00:04:28.384
Energy flow diagrams should distinguish
the route from the destination.

00:04:29.179 --> 00:04:29.964
Exactly.

00:04:30.304 --> 00:04:32.607
A store is a useful
accounting description.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.195
A pathway explains how energy moves.

00:04:35.576 --> 00:04:39.700
Mixing those two is a common exam
mistake that an arrow label can prevent

00:04:40.057 --> 00:04:40.080
A ball falls through a modest
height with negligible drag.
